  "surprise": "P24 reversed, d_ff 1024 -> 768 in all six Peri-LN blocks (4,012,032 params as registered; Muon QKV split keyed on qkv identity so fc1 (768,256) is still orthogonalized whole) on 115-fable scored 646/620/618 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115's 639/646/609: exact means 628.00 vs 631.33, -3.33, paired +7/-26/+9, inside the registered -35..+30 range and on its central -3. Discard (below the bar; the patch adds code, so no simplicity tie-break). The registered mechanism, less MLP memorization, is NOT supported: final train loss 0.052/0.054/0.053 is unchanged vs 115 (0.052), the train/val gap did not shrink (final val 0.087/0.083/0.084 vs 0.083), and throughput rose only 4-5% (4421/4385/4426 steps vs 4204/4218/4263, below the predicted 4,500-4,800; 3.65-3.68 epochs). Surprise: the RL trajectory changed shape. Round 1 was much weaker (targets 612/611/647 vs 718/756/691, mean -99; r1 sample acc 0.18-0.25 vs 0.32 on 115 s0), which falsifies the predicted >= 700, but expert iteration climbed faster (r1->r4 +530/+471/+464 vs +413/+366/+374) and RL-solved r4 finished level (1142/1082/1111, mean 1112 vs 1106). Eval tails were slightly thinner: >= 10 at 95/90/90 and >= 11 at 21/18/17 vs 103 and 25 on 115 s0, L* 12/11/11. Reading: MLP width, not memorization, sets the round-1 starting point here. Dropping a quarter of it costs the model length-7+ proofs it can sample before RL, and four RL rounds only win that back on RL-solved targets, not on dev >= 7. Neither direction of P24 (103: 5x -31, now 3x -3) beats 4x. Totals 1612/1549/1535 s.",
